       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day. That's double the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin (2,000 mg/day for extended-release). A single 1700 mg dose is also well above the usual maximum of about 1,000 mg. The overdose risk includes lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nThis may be a typo. Some possibilities:\n- **850 mg three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **500 mg or 1000 mg twice daily with meals**\n- **1700 mg total per day**, divided into doses such as 850 mg twice daily\n\nPlease tell me the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter the order right away. If you do want 1700 mg three times daily, please confirm it explicitly and I'll add a note documenting that it was intentional. I'd also suggest checking with pharmacy first."
