       "text": "I'm not going to enter this one, even with your confirmation. Metformin 5,100 mg/day has no recognized indication. It's twice the labeled maximum, and the 1700 mg single dose is well above what's studied or approved. The main risk is metformin-associated lactic acidosis, and normal kidney function doesn't protect against that at this dose. I can't enter it in good conscience, and I'd rather say so than leave you waiting.\n\nI can enter either of these right now:\n- **Metformin 850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **Metformin 1000 mg PO twice daily with meals** (2,000 mg/day), or a lower dose titrated up\n\nIf you have a clinical reason for going above the maximum, such as a specialist recommendation or a protocol, the order should go through your pharmacy and attending review. I can't enter it as written.\n\nTell me which of the options you'd like, or give me a different dose, and I'll enter it."
